Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report  MET FISH Analysis      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  59   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  YAW 9  BREAST ONC  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 13 43  Results To   Aditya Bardia MBBS  MPH  Joseph Misdraji MD    CLINICAL HISTORY   Breast Adenocarcinoma Metastatic to Gastrointestinal Tract  Liver     SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for MET    GROSS DESCRIPTION   1 block s  from Massachusetts General Hospital  the archived specimen was  retrieved and reviewed for adequacy    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID               TEST   MET FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST  Breast Adenocarcinoma Metastatic to Gastrointestinal Tract   Liver     SPECIMEN S  TESTED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA   United States     RESULTS     MET  hepatocyte growth factor receptor  copy number analysis     MET Chromosome 7 Reference Probe Copy Number Ratio  REMOVED_DATE    INTERPRETATION     The FISH data are consistent with NO amplification of the MET gene     TEST INFORMATION   Fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  using formalin fixed paraffin embedded  tumor specimens was used to analyze MET gene amplification status  Briefly   5 micron sections of formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor material were  prepared and an H E section reviewed to select regions for hybridization that  contain a majority of tumor cells  A dual color FISH assay was performed using  the REPEAT  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  C MET  7q31  Probe  chromosome 7q MET locus   Kreatech  and a copy number probe  centromere 7 or  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Abbott Vysis      Signal quantitation was used to generate a MET centromere 7 ratio  A ratio of  MET  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  of REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered borderline for amplification  A ratio  between REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification  A ratio greater than  5 0 or clustered MET signals that are too numerous to count would be considered  highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID  x 2     This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Center for Integrated Diagnostics   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Jackson  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Miguel N Rivera MD         PART   Molecular test for MET       report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
