left breast showed a 3 4cm non tender  ill defined  irregular  firm and  fixed mass     Ultrasound was used to evaluate the lesion and lesion that was ill defined   irregular  heterogeneously isoechoic and anechoic without significant internal  vascularity     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     2 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles without local anesthesia and  without complications   3 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by  David Hwang  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation was not discussed with the patient   Irene Kuter  M D  was notified of the preliminary results by e mail at 1 36 PM         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Rosemary H Tambouret MD on REMOVED_DATE 13 21       CLINICAL HISTORY  History of metastatic invasive ductal carcinoma  on Yeloda now with left breast  firmness for several months        SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 2 slides in ETOH  Received 3 air dried  slides  Received 3cc s of clear colorless fluid  One SurePath slide made           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
