asuring approximately 0 25cm on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   An immunostain for e cadherin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show positive staining in ductal cells supporting the diagnosis  however  the immunostained section is sub optimal due to fragmentation  The stain will be repeated and the results will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and right breast  is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram  25 x 17 x 5 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen  The anterior surface contains a 5 x 3 5cm skin ellipse with areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nipple that are grossly unremarkable  There is a stitch identifying the axillary tail  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis revealing no masses or lesions  The breast parenchyma is fibrous  No lymph nodes are appreciated  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of central portion of breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of upper inner quadrant  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and left breast  is a 27 x REMOVED_DATE x 6cm oriented  955 gram  left simple mastectomy specimen  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of skin extending medially from the skin ellipse and a 1 3cm x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple that are grossly unremarkable  There is a stitch orienting the specimen s axillary tail  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm circumscribed hemorrhagic cavity that has a heterogenous bloody and white cut surface in the central portion of the breast  The cavity measures 3 5cm to the closest posterior margin and 3cm to the closest anterior margin  Located 3 5cm superior medial to this cavity located in the upper inner quadrant  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm stellate firm lesion that is 3 2cm to the closest posterior and 3 1cm to the closest anterior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fibrous with areas of gray granular fibrous tissue and bright yellow discoloration located primarily in the upper inner and lower inner quadrants  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative radial section of closest posterior margin to the hemorrhage cavity in the central breast cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire cavity in the central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections to closest posterior margin for mass in upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass in upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of firm area in upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire firm bright yellow lesion in left inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of gray granular fibrous tissue from left inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nipple  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 24   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 12 29PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Addendum  1  Additional immunohistochemistry A repeated immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   demonstrates positive staining for ductal cells in areas of DCIS and negative staining in areas of invasive lobular carcinoma  The immunohistochemical staining pattern supports the previously reported diagnoses  Addendum  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 24   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 22 24PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
