 RIGHT  MASS  AND  SUPERO LATERAL  SPECIMENS   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  RIGHT   LATERAL  SPECIMEN   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue containing a pink tan firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The nodule is well demarcated and is present within 0 1cm to the closest inked margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  The remainder of the breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections from the specimen are submitted in cassettes A through G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Lateral mass  not from the mammography  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fatty tissue containing an irregular 0 5cm of papillary tan lesion present at the inked margin  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes H through J  Labeled  Right breast mass  superolateral  and consists of an irregular piece of fibrofatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a firm  tan pink nodule measuring 0 2cm in maximum dimensions  The rest of the breast tissue is predominantly fatty with intervening fibrosis  The nodule is submitted in cassette K and the remaining breast tissue is submitted in cassettes L and M  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFITLRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT SUPERO LATERAL   EXCISION   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
