ated with the scar   This superior site will be designated as site  1  1 5cm deep from scar  1   there is a red brown hemorrhagic biopsy cavity  3 x 1 x 1 5cm    which  approaches the deep resection margin by 0 7cm  There are no masses or focal  lesions associated with biopsy cavity  1   2cm directly lateral from the nipple  there is a 3 6cm well healed surgical  scar  which will be designated as scar  2  which is free of any nodularity or  ulceration  2cm deep to scar  2  there is a 2 x 2 x 1cm hemorrhagic and  fibrotic biopsy cavity  which approaches the deep resection margin by 0 3cm   At the inferior edge of this biopsy cavity  there is a 0 3cm in diameter hard  white nodule which is located greater than 1cm from both the superficial and  deep margins  There are no other focal lesions associated with the biopsy  cavity   The nipple is pink tan and unremarkable  without any areas of ulceration   dryness or discoloration  1cm directly deep to the nipple  however  there is  an ill defined area of tan white nodularity  2 x 2 x 1cm    which approaches  the deep margin by greater than 2cm   There is an incidental finding of a small pink tan skin lesion  0 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm   located 3 5cm from the lateral skin ellipse tip  and 3cm lateral to  the scar  2  This lesion is soft and slightly raised  and has a gross  appearance of a seborrheic keratosis   The axillary tail is removed and fixed in Bouin s solution prior to processing  for lymph nodes  Sixteen  16  possible lymph nodes are found   Represntative sections are submitted   Micro 1   8 possible lymph nodes  8 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  2 lymph nodes per cassette  multiple frags  RSS   Micro 6   nipple  2 frags  RSS   Micro 7   possible seborrheic keratosis  2 frags  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  section through nodular area deep to nipple  1 frag each  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy site  1 and overlying scar  1 frag each  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy site  1 and deep margin  1 frag each