mas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue as well as a needle localization wire  The fibroadipose tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in aggregate  Each piece is inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly fibroadipose parenchyma  however there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm ill defined stellate firm area which abuts the inked resection margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A   I  and the area previously described is submitted in A and B  Gross Description by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SUSPICIOUS AREA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Gus John Vlahakes  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
