howed an approximately 2 x 1cm non tender   well defined  ovoid  firm and mobile raised nodule     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     4 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   1 slide was stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by  Amy Ly  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  Michelle Specht  MD was notified of the preliminary results by text  message at 4 15 p m         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Amy Ly MD on REMOVED_DATE 15 49       CLINICAL HISTORY  Bilateral breast cancer  left breast nodule        SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 2 slides in ETOH and 1 air dried slide    B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  name and  medical number   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a collodion bag  Entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID            Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Specimen  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT       report_end  , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
