Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHAEL J YAREMCHUK  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 46 year old woman with a history of invasive ductal carcinoma of the left breast who is undergoing excision of a left breast mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL MASS   EXCISION  1  EXTENSIVE FAT NECROSIS WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  2  FOCAL FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL MASS   EXCISION  1  FAT NECROSIS WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left lateral breast mass   are 2 un oriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Each specimen is inked black and the smaller specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm ill defined nodule  focally abutting the black inked outer surface  The larger specimen is serially sectioned to reveal yellow gritty cut surfaces  with a focally indurated area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and focally abutting the black inked outer surface  The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller specimen  submitted entirely  indurated area in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger specimen  submitted entirely  indurated area in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left lateral breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm un oriented portion of fibroadipose tissue which is entirely inked black and sectioned to reveal ill defined fibrotic cut surfaces  with no definitive masses or lesions grossly identified  A representative section is submitted for Frozen Section as FX  1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   BREAST MASS  LEFT LATERAL   FAT NECROSIS  INFLAMMATION AND FOCAL CALCIFICATION  NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday February 03   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 06 30AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left Lateral Mass   Excision PART B  Breast  Left Lateral mass   Excision PART C  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only   report_end  , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 52 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal density right mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 2 3   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AND APPROACHING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED SURGICAL MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is no in situ component identified  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Receptor studies will be done on the formalin fixed tissue and reported separately  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies this specimen which indicates microcalcifications  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm stellate nodule REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in the center of the specimen which approaches to within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL FOR HORMOME BINDING ASSAY  AWAIT PERMANENT  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
