Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INFERIOR MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SCANT  LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH INVASIVE COMPONENT   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The margins of the resection appears free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO ONE LYMPH NODE  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 3 OF 7 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT ADDITIONAL AXILLA CONTENTS   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is an 8 x 5 x 3cm portion of breast tissue with a guide wire  A short suture designates the superior margin and a long stitch designates the lateral margin  The entire surface is inked black  with the anterior aspect overinked red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a hard  white nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  in the inferomedial portion of the specimen  coming within 0 3cm of the closest margin  inferior   No frozen section was done  The nodule in relation to closest inferior and anterior margins is submitted in cassettes A B  The remainder of the nodule in relation to inferior margin is submitted in cassette C  The remaining margins are grossly uninvolved  Sectioning through the parenchyma reveals predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue interspersed with a minute amount of delicate  fibrous tissue  Representative section of the sparse fibrous tissue is submitted in cassette D in relation to the anterior margin  and in cassette E in relation to the superior margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node  rule out met  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node 