D_ACCESSION_ID   Abbott Vysis      Signal quantitation was used to generate a MET centromere 7 ratio  A ratio of  MET  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  of REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered borderline for amplification  A ratio  between REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification  A ratio greater than  5 0 or clustered MET signals that are too numerous to count would be considered  highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID   morphometric analysis  in  situ hybridization  each probe  manual  x 1     This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Center for Integrated Diagnostics   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Jackson  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Miguel N Rivera MD         PART   Molecular test for MET       report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
