mas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm breast with a short stitch designating the superior edge and a long stitch designating the lateral edge  with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The overlying skin  REMOVED_DATE x 17 0cm  has a 1 0cm nipple with a 4 5cm areola  The nipple is focally hyperpigmented and firm  The areola is centrally hypopigmented  peripherally hyperpigmented and diffuse firm  The skin inferior and lateral to the nipple is firm  No definitive scar is identified on the skin  The breast is sectioned to reveal an irregular area of hard  stellate tissue with focal necrosis  located in the inferior breast  and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  This area is approximately 2 2cm from the anterior inferior margin and 4 0cm from the deep resection margin  The remaining parenchyma has lobules of fat interspersed with fibrous tissue  SECTION CODE  A  closest anterior inferior margin  B  closest anterior superior margin  C  closest deep margin  inferior  D  closest deep margin  nipple area  E F  representative sections of the tumor  inferiorly G H  representative sections of the tumor  superiorly  I  nipple  J K  medial areola  L M  representative sections of skin  medial to nipple  Dissected from the axillary tail  are multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  The lymph nodes are submitted in N through P  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Steven Joseph Nisco  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
