Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  SARAH P THAYER  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Adriana Dionigi Corben  M D  Frozen Section Consultant s   Judith A Ferry  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Olga Kolman  M D  Consulting Pathologist s   Robert Hasserjian  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Re excision right breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION  RARE ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  WHICH IS ALSO INVOLVED BY CHRONIC LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Two isolated tumor cells are identified on cytokeratin immunostains only  The frozen section slides do not demonstrate evidence of carcinoma  There is complete effacement of the lymph node architecture by small lymphocytes with clumped chromatin  round nuclei  inconspicuous nucleoli  and scant cytoplasm  Large cells are infrequent  Scattered residual germinal centers are noted  Immunohistochemical studies show diffuse strong positive staining for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with weak coexpression of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and patchy weak staining for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in the B cells  There is disorganized staining for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in residual follicle center dendritic cells  Ki67 reveals a proliferative index of about 15   with appropriately higher activity in the residual germinal centers  Staining for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is negative  Scattered small T cells are  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  These findings confirm the diagnosis of nodal involvement by the patient s known chronic lymphocytic leukemia  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH APOCRINE FEATURES  GRADE 3  SPANNI