Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 MAY 98 at 19 28 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    RE EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  10  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 98 at 11 20                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm brown lymph node with a small amount of attached adipose tissue  The lymph node is bisected and is entirely submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 2cm in greatest dimension up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  A section from each lymph node is submitted in cassettes B through D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm oriented breast biopsy specimen  There is an overlying skin ellipse  REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  on the anterior surface  oriented in a superior inferior direction  with a 2 0cm linear scar in the center of the skin ellipse  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior  to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm irregularly shaped  collapsed biopsy cavity in the center of the specimen  with surrounding yellow brown  hemorrhagic fat necrosis tissue  extending to the posterior resection margin on the superior half of the specimen  The entire specimen is inked black  the superior pole is overinked orange  and the lateral surface is overinked blue  and the posterior surface is overinked green  SECTION CODE E H  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity with margins  I K  Additional representative sections of a 1cm irregularly shaped  firm area adjacent to the biopsy cavity on the anterior resection margin  Recieved fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm aggregate of yellow fibroadipose tissue fragments  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes L through T  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    RE EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
