Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 25 CLINICAL DATA  Recurrent breast cancer  stitch 12 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RECURRENT INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN SKIN AND SUBAREOLAR TISSUE  SEE NOTE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN AND BEYOND THE REGION OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is noted in the dermis and subareolar region  All resection margins are negative for carcinoma  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 17 10                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 19     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     NOTE  This case is re examined at the request of Dr  Irene Kuter to establish the dimensions of the invasive component  The invasive tumor is present on 2 of 7 sections and is REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm as measured from slide A  It mostly involves the dermis of the nipple  The presence of ductal carcinoma in situ adjacent to the invasive component raises the possibility that this is a new primary tumor rather than a true recurrence  although the latter possibilty cannot be excluded  Lymphatic invasion is identified  but it is not extensive  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 02 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen  with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm tan skin ellipse  There is an eccentric 2 3cm areola with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm firm  flattened  tan red nipple  There is a 2 3cm scar arising 0 4cm superolateral to the nipple  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  The resection margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 9 x 3 7cm region of dense gray white fibrosis with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm region of diffuse hemorrhage deep to the nipple which comes to 1 0cm of the superficial margin and 2 5cm of the deep margin  The remaining cut surface is 70  tan yellow lobular and 30  gray white fibrous tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Hemorrhagic focus to nipple and deep margin B  Skin to hemorrhagic focus and superficial and deep margins C D  Hemorrhagic focus with surrounding fibrous tissue and skin E  Deep margin to hemorrhagic focus F G  Representative dense fibrous tissue away from hemorrhagic focus Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  LAN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Poor_(grade_III).
