Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Salima Shaikh  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA WITH PRIMARILY LOBULAR FEATURES  GRADE 2 OF 3  INNUMERABLE MICROSCOPIC FOCI ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RANGING IN SIZE FROM REMOVED_DATE TO REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  IN THE REGION OF THE INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   THE DISTANCES TO ALL EXAMINED MARGINS IS   REMOVED_DATE CM FOR BOTH IN SITU AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NO EVIDENCE OF ANGIOLYMPHATIC INVASION  HEALING BIOPSY SITES  2    BREAST AND AXILLA   METASTATIC MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 9 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  MICROMETASTASIS   NO EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION OR INVOLVEMENT OF AXILLARY VESSELS  ATYPICAL COLUMNAR CELL CHANGE AND FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  The vast majority of the invasive tumor in this material shows lobular features  Microscopic foci of invasive carcinoma are identified in 9 of 11 sections taken from around the healing biopsy site  which spans over 16cm   as well as in tissue away from the biopsy site  One 0 4cm focus of invasive carcinoma  also within the vicinity of the biopsy site  shows distinctly ductal features  and is suggestive of a separate primary  grade 1 of 3   Her 2 studies will be performed on this focus   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the results reported in an addendum  Hormone receptor and Her2 studies have been previously performed on the majority tumor  see addended report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE kg  40 5cm x 28 5cm x 5 4cm mastectomy specimen consisting of breast and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of paper labeled  3M Comp  also received with the specimen  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 22 4cm tan skin ellipse is notable for a 12 7cm linear scar in the right outer quadrant that is 2 8cm from the REMOVED_DATE x 5 6cm tan brown nipple areolar complex  A 4 4cm linear scar in the far right upper outer quadrant is located 1 6cm from the axillary tail  Three well circumscribed red telangiectatic areas measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm are located on the skin  1 4cm  8 2cm and 4 2cm respectively from the areolar complex  The posterior margin of the mastectomy specimen is smooth  and has scant strands of muscle and several small ligatures  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm healing biopsy site in the breast  deep to the 12 7cm linear scar  associated with scattered ill defined firm areas  The closest posterior margin to the breast biopsy cavity is 5 5cm  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm area of ill defined region of induration and fat necrosis in the axillary tail  consistent with healing biopsy site  deep to the 4 4cm linear scar near the axillary tail  and this area is 0 5cm from the posterior margin  The rest of the specimen reveals multiple fibrous areas  Six lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary region  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 4cm  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary biopsy site with closest deep posterior margin  9 5cm     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of axillary biopsy site to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast biopsy site changes in the more medial aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  include the anterior margin   Note   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Submitted medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face deep margin of breast biopsy cavity  5 5cm gross clearance    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast biopsy site  most suspicious areas in upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast biopsy sites  lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Deep margin to sections in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of medial breast  fibrous areas    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior breast   fibrous areas and cyst    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two intact candid lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One candidate lymph node  trisected  The axillary tail was re examined for potential additional lymph nodes and additional sections submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of the deep margin were also submitted  in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Salima Shaikh M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Salima Shaikh M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells of both invasive ductal and invasive lobular carcinoma do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleare