Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASS    INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen sction diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU PRESENT IN 3 OF 11 BLOCKS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   MASS    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm firm  tan white ill defined area  The entire lesion is submitted in cassette A through E  Representative sections of firm area adjacent to lesion in cassette F and G  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision   additional margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast  entirely submitted in cassettes H through M  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in N through R  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SUSPICIOUS AREAS  NOT LARGE OR HOMOGENOUS ENOUGH FOR FROZEN RECEPTORS  NO FROZEN TAKEN  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASS   PART B  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN   , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
