renchyma are submitted as follows  A   nipple B   representative skin C E   representative firmer parenchyma from the medial aspect F K   representative firmer parenchyma from the middle portion from medial to lateral L   closest inked lateral margin  inferior  M   closest deep margin N O   representative ________ parenchyma from the lateral aspect Labeled  left breast with axillary contents  is an 820 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm and overlying small REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm skin ellipse and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  The skin ellipse eccentrically contains a grossly unremarkable nipple  Six centimeters superior to the nipple is a 2 5cm long curved healing incision  Two sutures  one long designating the lateral aspect and one short designating the superior edge is present on the skin ellipse  One centimeters beneath the incision is 4 0cm in greatest dimension cystic space filled with blood clot  with an irregular  tan yellow  focally gelatinous inner surface  This cavity is located more superiorly in respect to the superior edge of the skin ellipse and is surrounded by up to 1 5cm thick  firm  irregular  tan yellow  gelatinous parenchyma  This parenchyma extends to within 0 2cm of the closest medial and superior lateral resection margin  0 3cm from lateral resection margin and 1 5cm from the deep margin  In addition  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm in greatest dimension irregular satellite area around the cavity contains firm  white tan  fibrous parenchyma with small cysts which is 2 0cm from the deep margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The axillary tissue contains several soft  tan lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm  Section Code P   nipple Q   skin with resent incision R   cavity closest to medial inked margin S   cavity closest to superior inked margin T   cavity closest to lateral inked margin U   deep margin V Y   rep