Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 43 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SPANNING A REGION ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY CRIBRIFORM TYPES  FORMING SMALL FOCI IN FOUR OF FOUR SECTIONS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm unremarkable breast biopsy specimen which is inked and sectioned to reveal yellow fatty tissue admixed with white rubbery tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through D  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESIONS IDENTIFIED  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
