Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Laboratory Report  Anti Neutrophil Cytoplasmic Antibody Testing      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  64   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  YAW  REMOVED_CASE_ID   RHEUMATOLOGY ASSOC  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 08 02  Results To   Sian Yik Lim MD      SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  BLOOD  147 250          SERUM  147 250  ANTI  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and ANTI MPO ANCA NEGATIVE  SEE NOTE     NOTE  Indirect immunofluorescence testing for anti neutrophil cytoplasm  antibodies  ANCA  shows a nuclear pattern of staining  which is not  characteristic of an ANCA associated vasculitis  ELISAs are negative for  anti proteinase 3 and anti myeloperoxidase antibodies     INTERPRETATION  The findings provide no support for the diagnosis of active  Wegener s granulomatosis  microscopic polyarteritis nodosa  related forms of  vasculitis or idiopathic necrotizing and crescentic glomerulonephritis  However   up to 40  of patients with limited Wegener s granulomatosis  i e  without  evidence of renal involvement  and up to 10  of patients with renal involvement  may be negative at presentation  Some of these will turn positive if tested  serially     The staining seen with this patient s serum may be due to antinuclear antibodies  or to other antibodies of unknown specificity and significance     Please call the MGH Immunopathology Laboratory at REMOVED_DATE with questions or  concerns regarding ANCA Tests     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Immunopathology Laboratory at the Massachusetts General Hospital  Their  characteristics have been published  Journal of the American Society of  Nephrology 2 27 36   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Human Pathology 24 170 8   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Archives of Internal  Medicine 156 440 5  Annals of Internal Medicine 126 866 73   REMOVED_CASE_ID   These test  have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration   FDA   The FDA has determined that clearance or approval is not necessary            Electronically Signed Out By  John L Niles MD         PART   BLOOD  147 250       report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
