Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 07 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   1 1 CM   WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 3   PRESENT AT INKED MARGINS ALONG A BROAD FRONT   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  PRESENT WITHIN AND ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED SURFACE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vessl or lymphatic space invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 98 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm white  firm  stellate area that is grossly at the inked margin  A representative section of the firm area is frozen as FX  1  now in cassette A  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in cassettes B and C  Representative sections of adjacent breast tissue submitted in cassettes D and E  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
